::Musical interval - a difference between two pitches.
These are, represented by the number of semitones they encompass:
0 - perfect unison (same note) 1 - minor second 2 - major second 3 - minor third 4 - major third 5 - perfect fourth 6 - diminished fifth/augmented fourth 7 - perfect fifth 8 - minor sixth 9 - major sixth 10 - minor seventh 11 - major seventh 12 - perfect octave::&lt;end&gt;

